// Third `SpriteSummon` wall in this folder -- see wall_of_sand.ron's
// header for the full write-up of the variant's real behavior. This
// spell's "deflects loose debris/small flyers/gusts" and the minor
// Bludgeoning-on-cross damage both drop for the same reason as the other
// two walls: `SpriteSummon` carries no attack/effect/aura field, so
// nothing it summons can deal damage or deflect projectiles -- the sheet's
// own notes already flag the damage as secondary ("the spell's primary
// function is a barrier"), which is exactly what a solid, riderless
// obstruction can still deliver honestly (an actual physical block via
// `solid_height`), even without the damage tick.
//
// No wind/air solid sprite exists in the terrain catalogue.
// `SpriteKind::SeaDecorPillar` (`solid_height: 2.55` --
// common/src/terrain/sprite/mod.rs) is used for the tallest available
// *solid* sprite among the reused sea-decor family (wall_of_water.ron
// picks `SeaDecorBlock` from the same family), approximating this spell's
// taller "5 m high" flavor better than a short/squat sprite would -- still
// a documented flavor drift, not a wind effect.
//
// The sheet's "15 m long, 5 m high" is the largest footprint of these
// three walls, so `summon_distance`/`angle` are widened accordingly
// relative to wall_of_sand.ron/wall_of_water.ron (both 9 m). `anchor:
// Target` matches the sheet's 37 m cast range.
SpriteSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.8,
    cast_duration: 0.6,
    recover_duration: 0.5,
    sprite: SeaDecorPillar,
    del_timeout: Some((58, 4)),
    summon_distance: (0, 4),
    sparseness: 0.25,
    angle: 120.0,
    anchor: Target,
    move_efficiency: 0.3,
    ori_modifier: 1.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(26.0)),
)
